WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.100
The energy pyramid followed only the tissue branch.

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.180
What happens to energy that never becomes tissue for the next level?

3
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:10.640
Return to the same Bay.

4
00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:15.640
Gold energy and green carbon now travel together, then separate.

5
00:00:19.183 --> 00:00:22.103
Sunlight enters the Bay as radiant energy.

6
00:00:23.523 --> 00:00:26.783
Phytoplankton change some into chemical energy in food.

7
00:00:28.543 --> 00:00:32.323
Consumers change food energy into movement, new tissue, and red heat.

8
00:00:33.703 --> 00:00:35.543
Energy is never made or destroyed.

9
00:00:36.783 --> 00:00:38.963
It changes form as organisms live.

10
00:00:40.017 --> 00:00:41.917
Heat spreads through water and air.

11
00:00:43.177 --> 00:00:47.077
No living thing can capture that dispersed heat to build food again.

12
00:00:48.337 --> 00:00:51.977
The gold path moves forward and fades outward as red ripples.

13
00:00:53.477 --> 00:00:57.377
Nearly every ecosystem needs a continuing energy supply.

14
00:00:58.597 --> 00:01:00.477
In the Bay, that supply is sunlight.

15
00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:04.990
A menhaden dies, and blue decomposers break it down.

16
00:01:06.270 --> 00:01:11.030
Can they return both its carbon and its usable food energy to phytoplankton?

17
00:01:12.230 --> 00:01:13.710
Hold both paths in mind.

18
00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:24.550
Decomposers release much of the menhaden's green carbon as carbon dioxide.

19
00:01:26.090 --> 00:01:28.290
Phytoplankton can take that carbon up again.

20
00:01:29.510 --> 00:01:31.350
The green path closes into a loop.

21
00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:39.950
Energy does not. Decomposers also respire, so more chemical energy becomes heat and

22
00:01:39.950 --> 00:01:41.690
leaves the usable food pathway.

23
00:01:42.783 --> 00:01:49.283
Compare the maps. Carbon atoms pass through organisms, air, and water, and can be

24
00:01:49.283 --> 00:01:52.923
reused. Some may be buried or carried away.

25
00:01:54.163 --> 00:01:57.383
Energy enters, changes form, and disperses as heat.

26
00:01:58.983 --> 00:01:59.983
Matter mostly cycles.

27
00:02:01.203 --> 00:02:03.863
Energy moves forward through this sunlit ecosystem.

28
00:02:05.083 --> 00:02:07.683
Not every ecosystem starts with sunlight.

29
00:02:08.983 --> 00:02:12.303
Some deep-sea vent communities begin with chemical energy.

30
00:02:13.443 --> 00:02:17.323
That changes the entrance, but energy still disperses as heat.

31
00:02:18.623 --> 00:02:22.383
The Bay picture has a clear scope, not a universal starting source.

32
00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:26.447
Ecologists test the picture with energy budgets.

33
00:02:27.647 --> 00:02:32.087
They compare neighboring feeding levels using matching measurements over the same

34
00:02:32.087 --> 00:02:38.227
area and time. Intake, new tissue production, and standing biomass are different

35
00:02:38.227 --> 00:02:42.367
measures. Mixing them makes a false transfer percentage.

36
00:02:43.450 --> 00:02:47.710
Transfer percentages vary among ecosystems and feeding steps.

37
00:02:49.370 --> 00:02:53.830
Temperature, what gets eaten, digestion, and respiration can change the share

38
00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:54.830
reaching new tissue.

39
00:02:56.010 --> 00:02:59.190
That variation does not turn energy into a cycle.

40
00:03:00.430 --> 00:03:05.010
It changes how wide the next gold band becomes before the remaining energy

41
00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:06.010
disperses.

42
00:03:06.733 --> 00:03:08.513
Return to the osprey's fish.

43
00:03:09.793 --> 00:03:15.133
Its carbon may later enter decomposers, carbon dioxide, and phytoplankton again.

44
00:03:16.493 --> 00:03:21.213
Its energy can power movement or growth only before becoming dispersed heat.

45
00:03:22.533 --> 00:03:26.893
The same organism belongs to a matter loop and a forward energy path.

46
00:03:27.883 --> 00:03:30.543
Keep paths separate when reading any food web.

47
00:03:31.783 --> 00:03:36.223
Energy flows through ecosystems, while matter cycles and can be reused.
